WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.770
SPEAKER: Thanks to
machine learning,

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.070
we can extract knowledge from
medical records, call center

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.210
conversations, medical voice
soundbites, medical forms,

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:13.560
regulatory filings, research
reports, insurance claims,

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.590
pharmaceutical
documentation, and more.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.200
This ultimately helps
doctors and care teams

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.260
get holistic views of
their patients quickly,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.870
or health plans to
see population trends

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.630
for their members, or
pharma to draw insights

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.670
from drug development research.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.670
This is possible thanks to a
field known as natural language

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.880
processing, which is concerned
with programming computers

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.870
to process and analyze large
bodies of human communication

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.240
that can live in many
different formats,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.630
such as written texts,
spoken utterances, or even

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.310
official documentation.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.160
And so in this episode, we
will share how organizations

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.100
can use one of Google's
natural language services

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.530
to specifically help
process structured

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.360
and unstructured
health care language

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.185
data using NLP, which stands
for Natural Language Processing.

00:01:01.185 --> 00:01:04.422
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.150
The Healthcare
Natural Language API

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.740
contains four key features that
help you find, assess, and link

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.420
knowledge in your data
in the following ways.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.750
For one, it has
the ability to text

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.610
to medical concepts,
which is referred

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.890
to as knowledge extraction.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.920
It also identifies and connects
related medical attributes,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.410
which is known as
relation extraction.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.660
It can also assess
surrounding factors

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.430
that could be
clinically relevant,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:37.000
known as context assessment, and
standardizes medical concepts

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.180
so they can be analyzed
across systems,

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.910
known as knowledge linking.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.890
Another way of
thinking about NLP

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.890
is that it can extract
critical clinical information,

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.500
like medications,
medical conditions,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.800
as well as understand
contexts, like negation,

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.160
such as, this patient
does not have diabetes.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.120
It also understands temporality,
such as, this patient will

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.080
start chemotherapy tomorrow,
and even infer there

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.940
are relationships
between things,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.960
such as side effects
or medication dosage.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.700
And what's most
notable is we have

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.370
a long list of ontologies
the natural language

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.050
models are trained with.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.780
Two notable ones
are the ICD, which

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.770
is used to code and classify
morbidity data from inpatient

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:26.760
and outpatient records,
physician offices, and most

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.090
National Center for
Health Statistics surveys.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.490
There's also SNOMED
clinical terms,

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:36.640
which provides core terminology
of electronic health records.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.150
The models also include
US official codes

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.940
for insurance
procedures and RxNorm,

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.210
which contains a list of
all medications available.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.330
Technical practitioners
can leverage healthcare NLP

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.030
to build apps for
their own organization

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.140
or for their entire industry,
such as enabling precise search

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.530
and discoverability across
patient populations,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.320
enable exchange of digital
health care information

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.100
and avoid processing delays,
establish and maintain

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.830
regulatory compliance,
or automate

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.310
administrative workflows, such
as identifying and eliminating

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.550
errors that require
corrective activities.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.640
Anyone who has science-based
texts around research

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:22.080
or clinical data can get value
from our Healthcare NLP API.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.690
Here are a few sectors that
can benefit to name a few.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:28.860
In telehealth, you now
have off-the-shelf support

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.160
for exchanging medical knowledge
captured in written form

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.340
and can extract structured
knowledge from texts

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.830
and make it available
for digital services,

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.580
such as chat bots, call centers,
clinical decision support

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.750
systems.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:46.200
This also frees up time
by triaging patient calls

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.470
and resolving cases that do
not require the intervention

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.270
of a clinical professional.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.400
Pharmaceutical
researchers are also

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.560
enabled via a standard
patient discovery

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.190
interface for population
health and R&amp;D applications,

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:02.100
since papers and clinical
trial documentation

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.950
can be surfaced to
match patients or find

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.330
novel treatments.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.460
Those managing
clinical trials can

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.680
both increase their
number of participants,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.560
as well as process the
high volume of feedback

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.860
and decrease time to
government approval.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.930
Users who manage
billing, especially

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.110
in insurance companies, can
have even better integration

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.200
with claims payment or
automate billing and coding

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.270
for insurance.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:29.280
You can enable
the Healthcare NLP

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:32.868
from your Google Cloud Projects
UI or via the command line.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:34.410
If you do not have
a project, there's

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.780
a link in the description along
with other helpful resources.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.330
And once you have
setup permissions

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.910
you can begin using its
context-aware models

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.490
to extract medical
entities, relations,

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.710
and contextual attributes.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.190
Each text entity is extracted
into a medical dictionary

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.060
entry.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.670
To extract medical,
texts make a POST request

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.420
and specify the following
information in the request.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.710
First, the name of
the parent service,

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.320
including the project
ID and location.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.730
Also, the target text.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.970
The maximum size is
10,000 Unicode characters

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.750
at this time.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.320
Let's quickly show you how
you can leverage the Natural

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.290
Language Healthcare API.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.710
We built a demo application
with a JavaScript frontend

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.860
to visually understand the
output of the Healthcare NLP

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.210
API.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.940
Let's test out the
sample medical record

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.110
for a hospital patient.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.760
We send over the
sample medical tests

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:38.403
to the API on the backend, and
we render the JSON response

00:05:38.403 --> 00:05:39.070
in this web app.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.070
In the first panel
down here, we can

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.380
see the various
entities extracted

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.450
and their corresponding
medical code.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.260
Next, we can see their diagnoses
with their corresponding

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:03.560
confidence scores.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.370
Now looking at the relationships
between the entities,

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.730
we can actually group
together important attributes.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.670
For example, take
a look at how long

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.770
and how much of
these medications

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.850
are taken or were prescribed.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.300
There are so many possibilities
when using Healthcare NLP,

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.090
and especially when you pair
it with Google services,

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:29.690
such as Dialogflow AI
for a chatbot interface.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:33.320
You can even build custom models
to build low-code apps using

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.930
AutoML Entity Extraction
for Healthcare,

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:38.930
so that users can simply
upload documents and then

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:42.590
perform manual annotations to
train and build a model on what

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:44.330
they would like to extract.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:48.380
This can then be integrated
into larger data pipelines.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.340
You can also use Document AI
to process faxed documents

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.980
or enable enterprise
search for life science

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.920
organizations using the
Google Knowledge Graph.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.290
To learn more about the
Healthcare Natural Language

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.155
API, you can visit
cloud.google.com

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:06.290
/healthercare/do
cs/concepts/nlp.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.910
And community, if you
found this episode helpful,

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.090
please subscribe to the
channel to get notifications

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.870
of more health care episodes.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:13.370
Cheers.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.720
